# Power Monitor with PID Braking Control

## Overview
This project implements an ESP32-based power monitoring system with PID-controlled braking. It measures voltage, current, and power using an INA226 sensor, displays readings on an OLED screen, and publishes data via MQTT. The system features automatic braking when voltage exceeds a threshold, controlled by a PID algorithm for precise regulation.

## Hardware Components
- ESP32 development board
- INA226 current/voltage sensor
- SH1106G OLED display (128x64)
- Braking circuit connected to PWM outputs
- WiFi connection
- MQTT broker

## Pin Configuration
| Component | ESP32 Pin |
|-----------|-----------|
| INA226 SDA | 18 |
| INA226 SCL | 19 |
| OLED SDA | 32 |
| OLED SCL | 33 |
| Brake Pin 1 | 14 |
| Brake Pin 2 | 25 |

## Features
- Real-time monitoring of voltage, current, and power
- OLED display with clear readings
- WiFi connectivity
- MQTT data publishing in JSON format
- PID-controlled braking system
- Multiple operation modes (GEN, BRAKE, IDLE)

## Software Dependencies
- Wire.h
- WiFi.h
- PubSubClient.h
- ArduinoJson.h
- Adafruit_GFX.h
- Adafruit_SH110X.h
- INA226.h
- PID_v1.h

## Setup Instructions
1. Create a `secrets.h` file with your WiFi and MQTT credentials:
   ```cpp
   #define WIFI_SSID "your_wifi_ssid"
   #define WIFI_PASS "your_wifi_password"
   #define MQTT_BROKER "your_mqtt_broker_ip"
   ```
2. Connect hardware according to the pin configuration
3. Upload the code to your ESP32
4. Ensure your MQTT broker is running

## MQTT Communication
- Published topic: `powermonitor/data` (contains voltage, current, power readings)
- Status topic: `powermonitor/status`
- Control topic: `powermonitor/setpoint` (to change braking threshold)

## Operation
The system monitors power parameters and automatically activates braking when voltage exceeds the setpoint (default 8.0V). The PID controller adjusts PWM duty cycle to maintain voltage at the desired level.

## Troubleshooting
- The system will retry INA226 initialization if it fails
- WiFi connection attempts timeout after 30 seconds
- MQTT reconnection is attempted automatically if connection is lost

